"description" = "Give your model and dataset folders a home on Hugging Face.\n\nFace Hugger brings local files, remote repositories, and upload activity into one native Mac workspace. Prepare a folder, review the destination, and start when you are ready.\n\nPREPARE WITH CONFIDENCE\nBrowse the local file preview, apply include and exclude filters, and see which previewed paths already exist remotely. File and folder conflicts are flagged before upload. Path checks do not claim that file contents are identical.\n\nKEEP TRANSFERS ORGANIZED\nQueue folders, follow reported preparation, upload or reuse, and commit activity, and stop or resume a transfer when needed. Already-committed files stay on Hugging Face. Saved folder–repository pairings make repeat uploads easier without starting them automatically.\n\nMANAGE THE BASICS\nBrowse model and dataset repositories, choose destination folders, create a repository with explicit public or private visibility, and delete individual remote files after confirmation.\n\nBUILT FOR YOUR MAC\nKeep uploads running when you close the window, return through the menu bar, and receive completion notifications. Optional sleep prevention keeps idle sleep from interrupting an active upload. Quitting the app stops the transfer; resume it when you return.\n\nA Hugging Face account with permission to write to your chosen repository and an internet connection are required for uploads. Matching remote paths may be replaced. Source folders remain live. If source files change, start a new upload so the updated contents can be reviewed.\n\nFace Hugger is an independent application, not an official Hugging Face product.";
"keywords" = "model,dataset,upload,repository,machine learning,developer,files,transfer,queue";
"promotionalText" = "Prepare model and dataset uploads in a native Mac workspace. Review files and destinations, save pairings, and manage your upload queue.";
